.esp-cache/
.esp-networks/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
results/*
# ...except the measurements themselves. These cost real provider budget and
# real hours; they are the evidence the report is built from, and a reader who
# clones this repository should be able to rebuild that report without paying
# for them again.
!results/history.json
!results/figures/
!results/figures/*.png

# The live cache is machine-local and quota-dependent. The committed
# measurements live in tests/fixtures/cache instead, so CI can reproduce them.
.esp-cache/

# The periodic verification writes a server log and a throwaway state dir.
.esp-verify.log
.esp-verify-state/

# A pasted API key. Never committed.
.env

# Generated from the service's state by scripts/serve_champion.py. Committing it
# would let a hand-edited copy drift from the genome that earned the score.
registries/champion.hocon
registries/champion_manifest.hocon

# One registry per measured network, plus their manifest, regenerated by
# scripts/serve_studio.py from the committed measurements. Generated for the
# same reason the champion is: a hand-edited copy would drift from the genome
# that earned the score, and then the thing being served would not be the
# thing that was measured.
registries/studio_*.hocon

# nsflow's own local database, created in the working directory the moment the
# accelerator UI starts. One deployment's chat history and session rows, and
# nothing another clone should inherit.
nss_local.db
nss_local.db-journal
logs/
state/champion.hocon

# One deployment's own runtime, which is never another deployment's.
#
# state.json is this machine's population and its per-day, per-model spend
# ledger. Committed, every clone would start up believing it had already
# measured candidates on somebody else's key and already spent today's budget.
# The measurements worth sharing are committed in tests/fixtures/cache, and
# scripts/adopt_measurements.py is how a fresh deployment picks them up.
#
# lease.json is a process lock. Lease.acquire only refuses while the recorded
# timestamp is inside ESP_LEASE_SECONDS, so a committed lease is worse than
# clutter: a clone would decline to run a wake for the rest of that hour,
# reporting that another optimiser holds a lease that no longer exists.
state/state.json
state/state.json.tmp
state/lease.json
state/lease.json.guard
